WEBVTT

welcome-1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.769
Hi Priya.

welcome-2
00:00:00.769 --> 00:00:04.231
This short video explains your mortgage offer from Fernmoor.

welcome-3
00:00:04.231 --> 00:00:06.154
It takes about two minutes.

welcome-4
00:00:06.154 --> 00:00:11.154
You can pause, turn on captions, or ask a question at any time.

your-loan-1
00:00:11.154 --> 00:00:14.615
You're borrowing £256,500 to buy a home worth £285,000.

your-loan-2
00:00:14.615 --> 00:00:16.923
That's 90 percent of its value.

your-loan-3
00:00:16.923 --> 00:00:19.615
Lenders call this your loan to value.

your-loan-4
00:00:19.615 --> 00:00:22.308
You'll pay it back over 30 years.

high-ltv-1
00:00:22.308 --> 00:00:26.923
Loans above 85 percent of a home's value usually have higher rates.

high-ltv-2
00:00:26.923 --> 00:00:30.385
Each payment you make lowers your loan to value.

high-ltv-3
00:00:30.385 --> 00:00:35.385
When your fixed rate ends, you may have more deals to choose from.

your-rate-1
00:00:35.385 --> 00:00:40.000
For the first 2 years, your rate is fixed at 4.89 percent.

your-rate-2
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.231
Your monthly payment stays at £1,359.76, even if interest rates change.

after-fixed-1
00:00:44.231 --> 00:00:47.308
Your fixed rate ends on 31 October 2028.

after-fixed-2
00:00:47.308 --> 00:00:50.769
After that, you move to our Standard Variable Rate.

after-fixed-3
00:00:50.769 --> 00:00:55.000
It's 7.49 percent today, and it can go up or down.

after-fixed-4
00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:00.000
If it stays the same, your payment would rise to £1,770.43 a month.

after-fixed-5
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.154
That's £410.67 more.

after-fixed-6
00:01:01.154 --> 00:01:05.385
Many people choose a new deal before their fixed rate ends.

overpayments-1
00:01:05.385 --> 00:01:12.308
You can pay off up to 10 percent of what you owe each year at no extra cost.

overpayments-2
00:01:12.308 --> 00:01:18.077
If you repay more than that during your fixed rate, there's an early repayment charge.

overpayments-3
00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:22.692
It's 2 percent in year 1 and 1 percent in year 2.

overpayments-4
00:01:22.692 --> 00:01:28.077
For example, repaying an extra ten thousand pounds in year 1 would cost £200.

total-cost-1
00:01:28.077 --> 00:01:33.846
Over the full 30 years, you'd repay about £627,498 in total, if rates don't change.

total-cost-2
00:01:33.846 --> 00:01:38.077
That includes your loan of £256,500 and the interest on it.

your-part-1
00:01:38.077 --> 00:01:41.538
There are a few things you need to do.

your-part-2
00:01:41.538 --> 00:01:43.077
Keep up your payments.

your-part-3
00:01:43.077 --> 00:01:46.154
Your home may be repossessed if you don't.

your-part-4
00:01:46.154 --> 00:01:47.692
Keep your home insured.

your-part-5
00:01:47.692 --> 00:01:51.538
And remember, this offer is valid until 14 March 2027.

contact-1
00:01:51.538 --> 00:01:56.923
If anything isn't clear, type a question in the box next to this video.

contact-2
00:01:56.923 --> 00:02:00.769
Or call us on 01632 960412 and quote your reference.

contact-3
00:02:00.769 --> 00:02:02.308
Thanks for watching, Priya.
